# Build context for the root Dockerfile is the repo root: it builds the client
# from apps/client and the API from apps/api into one image, so neither may be
# excluded here. `.git` stays for the same reason — the API build reads the
# commit out of it and links it in, so the image can report what it is serving.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
**/build
apps/api/bin
docker-compose*.yml
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docs
